From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgx-build <build@dgx-01.local>
Date: Sun, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] qwen3.8-flash-next: online MXFP8 weights for the
 hyper-connection mixers and the MoE router gate

The hyper-connection mixer is the largest dense weight stream in this model.
Per GatedResidual, two replicated BF16 projections:

  input_mix_weight_down_block_inject  [336, 10240]  6.88 MB  (merged, 12 pad)
  input_mix_weight_up                 [10240, 320]  6.55 MB

x 97 instances per decode step = 1303 MB per node, measured at 8.22 ms on
rank0 (98 c1 steps) -- 158 GB/s against a 273 GB/s LPDDR5x roofline, ahead of
the linear-attention projections (1.08 GB). The MoE router gate adds
[512, 2560] BF16 x 48 = 126 MB at 0.85 ms.

Both tensors are replicated on every rank (ReplicatedLinear /
MergedColumnParallelLinear(disable_tp=True)), so sharding them costs two
collectives per hyper-connection -- 194 per step -- for at best +2.2%. See
results/kernel-pass/lmhead-hc-design.md sections 4 and 5. Halving the stream
instead costs no collectives and no launches: quantize those weights to
MXFP8 g32 once at load and run them on b12x gemm.blockscaled, the kernel that
already serves this model MXFP8 linear-attention projections (9.16 ms/step for
243 launches).

Weight loading is untouched. maybe_route_hc_mxfp8 rebinds quant_method after
create_weights has already run, so the layer keeps its stock BF16
ModelWeightParameter, the MergedColumnParallelLinear shard loaders, the 12
alignment pad rows and _HC_WEIGHTS_MAPPER. The in-tree
Mxfp8OnlineLinearMethod then quantizes that loaded weight exactly once, in
process_weights_after_loading -- never per step -- and B12xMxfp8LinearKernel
packs it and registers the b12x preparation provider like every other MXFP8
linear here. Prefill, CUDA-graph capture and the launch count are unchanged;
only the bytes and the numerics move.

Activation precision is deliberately left to b12x
(VLLM_B12X_MXFP8_ACTIVATION_MODE / VLLM_B12X_DENSE_ACTIVATION_MODE, default
"auto"), which resolves it per exact-M regime: BF16 activations (W8A16) for
the decode regimes at M <= 8 where in_features == padded_in_features, and the
quantized-activation path at prefill capacity. Pinning "a16" as the LM-head
route does would pin b12x 16-row A16 tile for prefill as well, where the HC
mixers see the full batch and the LM head does not.

All three geometries clear b12x block-scaled contract: K % 32 == 0 and
N % 8 == 0 for [336, 10240], [10240, 320] (K padded to 384 by pack_weight),
[320, 10240] (the MTP mixer use_combine=False form) and [512, 2560].

NOT bit-identical: MXFP8 rounding is ~2^-8 relative per weight, so
scripts/logits_equiv.py fails by construction. Gated by VLLM_QWEN38_HC_MXFP8
(default "hc,gate"; "hc", "gate" or "off" to bisect) and judged on
scripts/gate_arm.sh. Mutually exclusive with
patches/vllm-qwen38-bf16-gemv.patch, which rebinds quant_method on the same
modules.

Applies on top of 8e1f1e587f.
---
